./" Manpage for ccv 
.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	ccv - cp a file, cd there, then edit it in vim (the copy not the original)
.SH SYNOPSIS
	ccv source destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	does cp, cds to wherever it is now, then edits the copied file in vim
.br
	only edits the last file if you give multiple
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose.
.br
	vim default options do not work
.SH EXAMPLES
	ccv hi.csv csvs
.br
	ccv sdifji.py ../../ijsdif/jsissbsbbsb.py
.SH BUGS
	probably none
